#{[17592186299902 :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+4y &=7 \\\\ 5x+2y &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-4$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-5$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $7$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-3$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-4$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-5$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-3$ |  |  |  |  |"] [17592186299903 :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+3y &=5 \\\\ 4x+y &=11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $5$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $11$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $11$ |  |  |  |  |"] [17592186299904 :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x &=y+5 \\\\ x-2 &=-3y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $5$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $2$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $2$ |  |  |  |  |"] [17592186299904 :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x-y &=5 \\\\ x+3y &=2.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 3-1\\cdot (-1)}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{13}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186299905 :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2y &=7-3x \\\\ x+1 &=-2y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $7$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-1$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ |  |  |  |  |"] [17592186299905 :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y &=7 \\\\ x+2y &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 2}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186299909 :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+8 &=0 \\\\ x &=7+3y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $-3$ | $0$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-1$ | {{field-2}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $7$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-3$ | $0$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $7$ |  |  |  |  |"] [17592186299909 :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+0y &=-8 \\\\ x-3y &=7.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-3)-1\\cdot 0}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{12}\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186299910 :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3y-2x &=5 \\\\ x &=-1-4y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $5$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-1$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-3$ |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $5$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ |  |  |  |  |"] [17592186299910 :question/worked-solution "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+3y &=5 \\\\ x+4y &=-1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{(-2)\\cdot 4-1\\cdot 3}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{11}\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"] [17592186299911 :question/problem "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=-1 \\\\ 4x &=6-y\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} |  | |  |  |  | |  | $-1$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $6$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} | $-2$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $-4$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  |\n|  | $-1$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $6$ |  |  |  |  |"] [17592186299911 :question/worked-solution "