17592186310032 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &=2u(t)+3v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=-u(t)+4v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310096 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &=2u(t)+3v(t)+1 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=-u(t)+4v(t)+2\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310103 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &={u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=2u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310153 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &={u}^{2}(t)+{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=-3u(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310156 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &={u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=-u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310325 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &={u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=2u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)-v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310397 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &=3u(t)-v(t)-1 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=2u(t)+v(t)+2\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310445 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &=2{u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+{v}^{2}(t)+3v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310468 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &={u}^{2}(t)+{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=2u(t)-v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310469 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &={u}^{2}(t)+2u(t)+{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=2u(t)+4v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310600 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &=3u(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310618 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &={u}^{2}(t)-u(t)+{v}^{2}(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=2u(t)+v(t)-3{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310673 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &=-3u(t)+v(t)+5 \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=2u(t)+5v(t)-9\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310727 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &=2{u}^{2}(t)+2v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=4u(t)-2{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310728 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &=3u(t)-v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=2u(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310738 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &=2{u}^{2}(t)+u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310763 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &={u}^{2}(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=2{u}^{2}(t)-v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186310768 :answer/value "\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &={u}^{2}(t)+u(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=-3u(t)-{v}^{2}(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right."] [17592186311544 :question/problem "Consider the following initial value problem for the functions $y=y(x),z=z(x),w=w(x):$\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} &=x+y+{w}^{2},\\, && y(0)=1 \\\\ {z}^{′} &=2y-z,\\, && z(0)=2 \\\\ {w}^{′} &=-w+xz,\\, && w(0)=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWe wish to approximate the solution using Euler's method.\nWhat entries should be placed in the columns for $Δy,$ $Δz,$ and $Δw$ in the table below if the step size is $Δx=1?$\n\n| $x$ | $y$ | ${y}^{′}$ | $Δy$ | $z$ | ${z}^{′}$ | $Δz$ | $w$ | ${w}^{′}$ | $Δw$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  | {{field-3}} |\n\nTherefore, $y(1)≈$\n{{field-4}},\n$z(1)≈$\n{{field-5}},\nand $w(1)≈$\n{{field-6}}."] [17592186311545 :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the derivative of $r(t):$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t-1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $r(t)$ are parallel for some specific value ${t}_{0}$ of the parameter $t$ if and only if there exists a constant $c$ such that $r({t}_{0})=c\\,{r}^{′}({t}_{0}).$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(t) & =c\\,{r}^{′}(t) \\\\ ⟨{t}^{3}\\,,\\,{e}^{t}\\,,\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩ & =c\\,⟨3{t}^{2},\\,{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{t-1}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nEquating the components gives:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{t}^{3} &=c(3{t}^{2}) \\\\ {e}^{t} &=c{e}^{t} \\\\ {e}^{t-1} &=c{e}^{t-1}\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFrom the second and third equations, we obtain that $c=1.$ Substituting $c=1$ into the first equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{3} & =3{t}^{2} \\\\ {t}^{3}-3{t}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {t}^{2}(t-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, $r$ and ${r}^{′}$ are parallel only at the points corresponding to $t=0$, and $t=3.$\n\nFinally, since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r(0) & =⟨{0}^{3},\\,{e}^{0},\\,{e}^{0-1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,{e}^{-1}⟩ \\\\ r(3) & =⟨{3}^{3},\\,{e}^{3},\\,{e}^{3-1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨27,\\,{e}^{3},\\,{e}^{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n we conclude that $r(t)$ and ${r}^{′}(t)$ are parallel at the points $(0,1,{e}^{-1})$ and $(27,{e}^{3},{e}^{2}).$"] [17592186311546 :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)-y(t)+5 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=2x(t)+y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. The equilibrium point of the system is $[-1,\\,2]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting the equilibrium to the origin?"] [17592186311546 :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere $x=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nTo shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗},\n$$\n\nwhere $u=\\begin{bmatrix}u(t) \\\\ v(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,⇒\\,x=u+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x$ and ${x}^{′}$ into the given system, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′} & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}(u+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix})+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}u+\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}u+\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &=3u(t)-v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=2u(t)+v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186311547 :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=2x(t)+3y(t)+4 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-x(t)+4y(t)+9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. The equilibrium point of the system is $[1,\\,-2]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting the equilibrium to the origin?"] [17592186311547 :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere $x=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nTo shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗},\n$$\n\nwhere $u=\\begin{bmatrix}u(t) \\\\ v(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,⇒\\,x=u+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x$ and ${x}^{′}$ into the given system, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′} & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}(u+\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix})+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}u+\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}u+\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &=2u(t)+3v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=-u(t)+4v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186311548 :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-3x(t)+y(t)+5 \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=2x(t)+5y(t)-9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nConsider the system of ODEs above. The equilibrium point of the system is $[2,\\,1]^{T}.$ Which of the following is the system obtained by shifting the equilibrium to the origin?"] [17592186311548 :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\nwhere $x=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nTo shift the system's equilibrium from ${x}^{∗}$ to the origin, we define the deviation vector\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗},\n$$\n\nwhere $u=\\begin{bmatrix}u(t) \\\\ v(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nIn our case, we have\n\n$$\nu=x-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,⇒\\,x=u+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\\,\\text{and}\\,{x}^{′}={u}^{′}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x$ and ${x}^{′}$ into the given system, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}x+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\ {u}^{′} & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}(u+\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix})+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}u+\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}u+\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}u.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the shifted system is the following:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(t) &=-3u(t)+v(t) \\\\ {v}^{′}(t) &=2u(t)+5v(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$"] [17592186311559 :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-5x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"150px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>"] [17592186311560 :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-7y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=7x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ 